       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant.\n\nCould you tell me which of these you meant?\n\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** I could enter 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **A different per-dose amount.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum. 500 mg or 1,000 mg are also common doses.\n- **The dose is correct as written.** If so, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. Your pharmacy will probably want to verify it too.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order."
