     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA label doesn't support the premise you gave.\n\n- **Immediate-release metformin:** the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, and 1,000 mg is the usual maximum single dose. The label says doses above 2,000 mg/day may be better tolerated when divided three times daily.\n- **Extended-release metformin:** the labeled maximum is 2,000 mg/day, or 2,500 mg/day for Glumetza/Fortamet-type formulations.\n- **The order as written:** 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum, so it is outside the label.\n\nI can't enter it on the basis that it's within label. I may be missing something, such as a different formulation or a typo in the dose or frequency. If so, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order. Some options:\n\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 850 mg PO twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, I need you to confirm that you know it exceeds the labeled maximum and that you're prescribing it as an intentional off-label dose. Then I can enter it with a note saying so, and pharmacy can review it."
      }
     ],
